    "result_text": "Both acceptance tests pass. \n\nSummary of the change:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setMembershipTier` setter.\n\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 the one function that builds the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response. It already computed `namesakeCount`; I captured it in a local and set the tier: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0 && owner.getEmail() != null`, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nKept structural impact low: the logic lives inline in the single-method `RespondWithOwner` class (`WMC_other = 1`), reusing the already-computed `namesakeCount` rather than adding a new class, and touching only two files.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE) both green.",
